# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 124-126 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 13 — CHAPTER 15, 2026-09-22; RUN B2, THE SECOND HALF): the firstling — its year, the
# blemished, the shearing and the work, the consecrated by a refuted a fortiori, "you shall sanctify" against "no man shall sanctify", the ox and the flock
# crossed (124), the two days of "year by year" (125), the blemish born and acquired, lame and blind the paradigm, the blood — drinking, the warning, the
# olive, the ground, the pouring (126) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation CUT by consonants from the print's letters
# (ch15_ink.SP_); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, checked before typed: I1 the a fortiori, I8 the particular that teaches
