from ch15_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(124, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY FIRSTLING THAT IS BORN IN YOUR HERD" (15:19) — IT TELLS THAT THE FIRSTLING IS EATEN ALL ITS YEAR. I HAVE ONLY THE UNBLEMISHED FIRSTLING; WHENCE THE BLEMISHED? "EVERY FIRSTLING". SINCE IT IS SAID "YOU SHALL NOT WORK WITH THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR OX NOR SHEAR THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR FLOCK", IT TEACHES THAT THE FIRSTLING IS FORBIDDEN IN SHEARING AND IN WORK. I HAVE ONLY THE UNBLEMISHED; WHENCE THE BLEMISHED? "EVERY FIRSTLING". The head row of piska 124 ({SP_(124, 1, "שהבכור", "נאכל", "כל", "שנתו")} "that the firstling is eaten all its year"; {SP_(124, 1, "אסור", "בגזה", "ובעבודה")} "forbidden in shearing and in work"): THE YEAR, THE BLEMISHED AND THE TWO BARS FROM "EVERY" — the firstling\'s year read from the head verse with 15:20\'s "year by year" (the English cites both), the blemished firstling inside every clause; the exam: Mishnah Bekhorot 4:1, Bekhorot 25a-28b. Fresh.')
srow(124, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT IS BORN" — TO THE EXCLUSION OF THE ONE BORN BY THE SIDE. ({SP_(124, 2, "פרט", "ליוצא", "דופן")} "to the exclusion of the one born by the side"): THE BIRTH\'S WAY A CONDITION — the caesarean not "born" (Mishnah Bekhorot 2:9 the English\'s note; 101:2\'s list at chapter 14 had the same creature among the altar\'s disqualified). Fresh.')
srow(124, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN YOUR HERD AND IN YOUR FLOCK, THE MALE YOU SHALL SANCTIFY TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — IT TEACHES THAT THE FIRSTLING IS EATEN ALL ITS YEAR. I HAVE ONLY THE FIRSTLING; WHENCE TO INCLUDE ALL THE OTHER CONSECRATED? "EVERY FIRSTLING". SINCE IT IS SAID "YOU SHALL NOT WORK … NOR SHEAR", THE FIRSTLING IS FORBIDDEN IN SHEARING AND WORK; WHENCE ALL THE OTHER CONSECRATED? IT IS A REASONING: IF THE FIRSTLING, WHICH DOES NOT APPLY TO EVERY OFFSPRING AND GOES OUT TO COMMON USE WITHOUT REDEMPTION, IS FORBIDDEN IN SHEARING AND WORK — THE CONSECRATED, WHICH APPLY TO EVERY OFFSPRING AND GO OUT ONLY BY REDEMPTION, IS IT NOT LOGICAL THAT THEY BE FORBIDDEN? NO: IF YOU SAID IT OF THE FIRSTLING, WHOSE HOLINESS IS FROM THE WOMB AND FALLS EVEN ON A PERMANENT BLEMISH, WILL YOU SAY IT OF THE CONSECRATED, WHOSE HOLINESS IS NOT FROM THE WOMB AND DOES NOT FALL ON A PERMANENT BLEMISH? WHENCE? "YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK YOU SHALL SANCTIFY, AND YOU SHALL NOT WORK NOR SHEAR". ({SP_(124, 3, "לרבות", "שאר", "כל", "הקדשים")} "to include all the other consecrated"; {SP_(124, 3, "שקדשתו", "מרחם")} "whose holiness is from the womb"): I1 (checked) FROM THE FIRSTLING TO ALL THE CONSECRATED, REFUTED BY THE WOMB\'S HOLINESS, THEN THE VERSE — 71:6\'s form at 12:15 (the outside row) with the same two features; the exam: Bekhorot 25a. Fresh.')
srow(124, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL SANCTIFY TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — R. ISHMAEL SAYS: ONE VERSE SAYS "YOU SHALL SANCTIFY" AND ONE VERSE SAYS "NO MAN SHALL SANCTIFY" (LEVITICUS 27:26). [ONE CANNOT SAY "SANCTIFY", FOR IT IS SAID "DO NOT SANCTIFY"; ONE CANNOT SAY "DO NOT SANCTIFY", FOR IT IS SAID "SANCTIFY". SAY THEN: YOU SANCTIFY IT AS A VALUATION-CONSECRATION, YOU DO NOT SANCTIFY IT] AS AN ALTAR-CONSECRATION. MIGHT IT BE EVEN A CONSECRATION FOR THE HOUSE\'S REPAIR, WHICH IS NOT AN ALTAR-CONSECRATION? "THE FIRSTLING" — AS THE FIRSTLING IS PARTICULAR AS AN ALTAR-CONSECRATION [SO EVERY ALTAR-CONSECRATION]. OR — WHAT YOU LEARN BY ONE WAY YOU LEARN BY ALL ITS WAYS: AS THE FIRSTLING IS PARTICULAR AS A LESSER HOLY THING, EATEN FOR TWO DAYS, AND PRACTICED IN YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK — I INCLUDE ONLY ITS LIKE! WHENCE TO INCLUDE THE MOST HOLY AND THE LESSER HOLY OF THE INDIVIDUAL AND OF THE COMMUNITY? "IN YOUR HERD AND IN YOUR FLOCK … YOU SHALL SANCTIFY, YOU SHALL NOT WORK … NOR SHEAR". THE FIRSTLING WENT OUT ONLY TO TEACH YOU: AS THE FIRSTLING IS PARTICULAR AS AN ALTAR-CONSECRATION — OUT GOES THE CONSECRATION FOR THE HOUSE\'S REPAIR, WHICH IS NOT AN ALTAR-CONSECRATION. ({SP_(124, 4, "כתוב", "אחד", "אומר", "תקדיש")} "one verse says you shall sanctify"; {SP_(124, 4, "הקדש", "מזבח")} "an altar-consecration"; {SP_(124, 4, "בדק", "הבית")} "the repair of the House"): THE DESIGN\'S CONTRADICTION RESOLVED BY THE SHELF — "you shall sanctify" (15:19) and "no man shall sanctify it" (Leviticus 27:26, the kin\'s ledger) TWO VERSES UPHELD BY DIVIDING THE SPHERES (I13\'s question, the resolution a distinction — no third verse; no code claimed): the firstling sanctified for its VALUE (the treasury), never for the altar (it is the altar\'s from the womb) — Mishnah Arakhin 8:7 the English\'s note (13b\'s testing shelf); then THE FIRSTLING SINGLED OUT TO TEACH THE CLASS (I8\'s shape): every altar-consecration under the shearing and work bars, the House\'s-repair consecration out; the bracketed text one editor\'s (the English\'s note on the Vilna Gaon\'s reformulation). Fresh.')
srow(124, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH SAYS: "YOU SHALL NOT WORK WITH THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR OX" — YOU MAY WORK WITH THAT OF OTHERS; "NOR SHEAR THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR FLOCK" — YOU MAY SHEAR THAT OF OTHERS. R. SHIMON SAYS: "YOU SHALL NOT WORK WITH THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR OX" — YOU MAY WORK WITH A HUMAN FIRSTBORN; "NOR SHEAR THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR FLOCK" — YOU MAY SHEAR THE FIRSTLING OF AN ASS. ({SP_(124, 5, "עובד", "אתה", "בשל", "אחרים")} "you may work with that of others"; {SP_(124, 5, "בבכור", "אדם")} "with a human firstborn"; {SP_(124, 5, "פטר", "חמור")} "the firstling of an ass"): "YOUR" READ TWO WAYS — the gentile\'s firstling (R. Judah) or the human and the ass (R. Shimon: Exodus 13:13\'s ass and the firstborn son the kin by name, no Onkelos row of them in any ledger, asserted) — a DISPUTE on the possessive; the English\'s row runs on into 124:6\'s reasoning (the two files divide the piska differently — both read whole). Fresh.')
srow(124, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY THE OX\'S FIRSTLING IN WORK AND THE FLOCK\'S IN SHEARING; THE OX\'S IN SHEARING AND THE FLOCK\'S IN WORK, WHENCE? YOU REASON: IF WHERE THE BLEMISHED OF THE HERD IS NOT EQUAL TO THE UNBLEMISHED OF THE HERD FOR THE ALTAR, IT IS EQUAL TO IT IN WORK — WHERE THE UNBLEMISHED OF THE FLOCK IS EQUAL TO THE UNBLEMISHED OF THE HERD FOR THE ALTAR, IS IT NOT LOGICAL THAT IT BE EQUAL IN WORK? AND THE SAME FOR SHEARING. AND WE HAVE LEARNED ONLY THE UNBLEMISHED; THE BLEMISHED, WHENCE? [THE SAME TWO REASONINGS ON THE BLEMISHED.] THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT WORK WITH THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR OX NOR SHEAR THE FIRSTLING OF YOUR FLOCK". ({SP_(124, 6, "והוא", "הדין", "לגזה")} "and the same for shearing"; {SP_(124, 6, "בעלי", "מומים", "מנין")} "the blemished, whence"): I1 (checked) FOUR TIMES — the two bars crossed over the two kinds and then over the blemished, each by an a fortiori from the altar\'s equality to the work\'s; THE TWO FILES READ THE CLOSING VERSE OPPOSITE WAYS — the Hebrew\'s "the Teaching says" seals the extension, the English\'s bracket reads it as a limit (cattle by work alone, sheep by shearing alone): a DISPUTE of the two files, the exam\'s to settle (Bekhorot 25a; Mishnah Bekhorot 3:3-4). Fresh.')
srow(125, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL EAT IT YEAR BY YEAR" (15:20) — IT TEACHES THAT THE FIRSTLING IS EATEN FOR TWO DAYS: ONE DAY OF THIS YEAR AND ONE DAY OF THE COMING YEAR. The one-row piska ({SP_(125, 1, "נאכל", "לשני", "ימים")} "eaten for two days"; {SP_(125, 1, "לשנה", "הבאה")} "and of the coming year"): "YEAR BY YEAR" READ AS A DAY ON EACH SIDE OF THE YEAR\'S EDGE — the firstling\'s two days (Mishnah Zevachim 5:8 the English\'s note; 124:4\'s "eaten for two days" the same datum), the phrase the Torah\'s two — the firstling here and the hireling of Leviticus 25:53 (asserted); 106:5\'s "the year passed" the outside row on the same clock. Fresh.')
srow(126, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF THERE BE IN IT A BLEMISH" (15:21) — I HAVE ONLY ONE BORN UNBLEMISHED THAT BECAME BLEMISHED; ONE BORN BLEMISHED FROM ITS MOTHER\'S WOMB, WHENCE? "ANY EVIL BLEMISH". WHENCE THE SCABBED, THE WARTED AND THE ONE WITH TUMORS, THE OLD, THE SICK AND THE FOUL? "BLEMISH, ANY EVIL BLEMISH, YOU SHALL NOT SACRIFICE IT". MIGHT HE NOT SLAUGHTER THEM IN THE SANCTUARY BUT SLAUGHTER THEM IN THE PROVINCES? "LAME OR BLIND" — LAME AND BLIND WERE IN THE GENERAL; WHY DID THEY GO OUT? TO COMPARE TO THEM: AS LAME AND BLIND ARE PARTICULAR — A BLEMISH IN THE OPEN THAT DOES NOT PASS — SO I HAVE ONLY A BLEMISH IN THE OPEN THAT DOES NOT PASS. The head row of piska 126 ({SP_(126, 1, "נולד", "בעל", "מום", "ממעי", "אמו")} "one born blemished from its mother\'s womb"; {SP_(126, 1, "בכלל", "היו", "ולמה", "יצאו")} "were in the general; why did they go out"; {SP_(126, 1, "מום", "שבגלוי", "ואינו", "חוזר")} "a blemish in the open that does not pass"): I8 (checked) IN ITS OWN WORDS — LAME AND BLIND THE PARTICULARS THAT TEACH THE CLASS: visible and permanent, the two features of every disqualifying blemish (71:6\'s "permanent blemish" at 12:15 the same rule from the other verse); the born-blemished and the diseased in by "any"; the provinces\' slaughter asked and barred by the paradigm; 147:3-4 the same words at 17:1 (the English\'s note); the exam: Mishnah Bekhorot 6, Bekhorot 33a-37b. Fresh.')
srow(126, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY ITS BLOOD YOU SHALL NOT EAT" (15:23) — DRINKING IS INCLUDED IN EATING. ({SP_(126, 2, "שתיה", "בכלל", "אכילה")} "drinking is included in eating"): THE VERB\'S REACH — the blood\'s bar by "eat" covers the cup; 12:16 and 12:23\'s clauses at their third seat (asserted); the row cites 15:23 inside piska 126 (the spine\'s last citation of the chapter). Fresh.')
srow(126, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY" — THIS IS THE WARNING OF WITNESSES. ({SP_(126, 3, "זו", "התרית", "עדים")} "this is the warning of witnesses"): THE LIMITING PARTICLE READ AS THE COURT\'S CONDITION — no lashes without a forewarning (the exam: Makkot 3b lists the release\'s witnesses too); the compile: the penalty gated. Fresh.')
srow(126, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY" — TO GIVE THE MEASURE OF AN OLIVE THAT THE TORAH SAID. ({SP_(126, 4, "שיעור", "כזית")} "the measure of an olive"): THE THRESHOLD — the olive\'s bulk the liability\'s quantity (Keritot 20b-22a\'s blood classes at chapter 12\'s docket the kin); a quantity for the data channel. Fresh.')
srow(126, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON THE EARTH" — AND NOT INTO A PIT, NOR INTO A HOLE, NOR INTO RUNNING WATER AND RIVERS; RATHER HE GOES INTO HIS HOUSE AND SLAUGHTERS BESIDE A HOLE, AND THE BLOOD RUNS DOWN INTO THE HOLE SO AS NOT TO SOIL THE WHOLE HOUSE; AND IN THE MARKET HE SHALL NOT DO SO, LEST HE IMITATE THE SECTARIANS. ({SP_(126, 5, "ולא", "על", "הגמא")} "nor into a hole"; {SP_(126, 5, "שלא", "יחקה", "את", "המינים")} "lest he imitate the sectarians"): THE GROUND AND NOT THE PIT — the pouring\'s place a rule against the look of an offering (Mishnah Chullin 2:9 the English\'s note; the house permitted, the market barred); the compile: the blood\'s disposal a place condition with an exception. Fresh.')
srow(126, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL POUR IT" — POURING IS ONLY FROM THE NECK. R. ELIEZER SAYS: "ON THE EARTH YOU SHALL POUR IT AS WATER" — AS WATER MAKES SEEDS SUSCEPTIBLE, SO THE BLOOD OF SLAUGHTER MAKES SEEDS SUSCEPTIBLE. OR THE BLOOD OF STABBING, OF TEARING, THE SPURTING, THE LET BLOOD, THE SPLEEN\'S, THE FETUS\'S AND THE RESIDUE, THE LIVER\'S, THE HEART\'S AND THE BLOOD OF DEATH — ARE THEY MEANT? "YOU SHALL POUR IT AS WATER" — WHAT IS POURED AS WATER MAKES SUSCEPTIBLE; OUT GO THESE, WHICH DO NOT. ({SP_(126, 6, "אין", "שפיכה", "אלא", "מן", "הצואר")} "pouring is only from the neck"; {SP_(126, 6, "מכשירים", "את", "הזרעים")} "make seeds susceptible"): THE COMPARISON "AS WATER" READ AS A LAW OF UNCLEANNESS — the blood of slaughter a liquid that prepares food for impurity, the other bloods not (Mishnah Makhshirin 6:8, Tosefta Makhshirin 3:14 the English\'s notes; the English\'s note: a medieval copyist\'s block by one editor); the pouring the neck\'s — the slaughter\'s own blood; the chapter\'s last row. Fresh.')
